- 2007: Start of development: Robert Griesemer, Rob Pike and Ken Thompson
- 2009: First public presentation
- 2012: Version 1
- 2014: First Gopher conference

* Why Go?
- Go is the major language behind the Cloud Native Stack
.link https://www.cncf.io/
.image ./img/01-cncf-projects.png 100 1024
- The most important components are written in Go: Docker, Kubernetes, etcd, Prometheus, Grafana, ...
- Go is open source and maintained by Google
- Go was designed at Google for concurrent systems programming, to address problems of large C++ code bases (slow builds, complexity).

